# Styloviz

Standalone Angular components on Tailwind CSS 4. Free: `@styloviz/<name>`. Pro:
`@styloviz-pro/<name>`. Docs: https://styloviz.dev/docs

- Before using a component, look up its exact API with the `styloviz` MCP server
  (`search`, then `get_component`) — or `npx -y @styloviz/mcp component <name>`.
  Never guess input names. Add the server in `.cursor/mcp.json`:
  `{ "mcpServers": { "styloviz": { "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "@styloviz/mcp"] } } }`
- Global CSS: `@import "tailwindcss"; @import "@styloviz/core/styles/styloviz.css";`
  plus `@source "../node_modules/@styloviz";` (and `@styloviz-pro` for Pro).
- `provideStyloviz()` in `app.config.ts`; dark mode is the `dark` class on `<html>`.
- Standalone only: import the component class into `imports`. No NgModules.
- Register glyph names you pass in: `provideSvIcons([bellIcon])`,
  `import { bellIcon } from '@styloviz/icons/glyph/bell'`.
- Form controls are ControlValueAccessors: `formControlName`, `[(ngModel)]`, `[formField]`.
- Strings come from label packs: `provideSvLabels(SV_<PACKAGE>_LABELS_<LANG>)`, `provideSvLocale()`.
- Use kit tokens (`bg-primary-600`, `dark:` variants), not hex.
- Controls under 24 px: add `sv-target`. Sticky page header: `data-sv-sticky="page-top"`.
  Scroller with sticky bands: `svRevealFocus` + `data-sv-sticky` on each band.
  Anything draggable needs a tap alternative (WCAG 2.5.7).
